        "original_id": "a384a8f5-9e46-5494-89ff-fa0009fdc880",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ted Kennedy, John F. Fitzgerald, John F. Kennedy, M.T. \"Nuf Ced\" McGreevy, M.J. Regan, Rose Kennedy\n- Organizations: Royal Rooters\n- Places: Doyle's Cafe\n- Roles: Boston Mayor, senator, chairman, secretary\n- Events: St. Patrick's Day 1988 dedication\n\nFacts:\n- John Francis \"Honey Fitz\" Fitzgerald was born on February 11, 1863, and died on October 2, 1950.\n- John F. Fitzgerald was an American politician, the father of Rose Kennedy, and the maternal grandfather of President John F. Kennedy.\n- M.T. \"Nuf Ced\" McGreevy was the spiritual leader of the Royal Rooters.\n- John F. Fitzgerald, who was Boston Mayor and the maternal grandfather of John F. Kennedy, served for a time as chairman of the Royal Rooters.\n- During John F. Fitzgerald's time as chairman of the Royal Rooters, M.J. Regan served as the organization's secretary.\n- On St. Patrick's Day in 1988, Senator Ted Kennedy helped dedicate a new room at Doyle's Cafe to his maternal grandfather, John F. Fitzgerald.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
